Three edits. Nothing else in the file changes, and nothing is reordered.

(1) Replace this block — the 21-line comment and the six-selector rule, at src/web/styles.css:364-392 — with the new text in its place:

--- OLD
/* A free-text name on an experiment, opportunity or approval is one
   unbreakable token, and one long enough token still scrolls the whole page
   sideways even with the floor lifted above. The reason is a level down from
   where #48 fixed it: #main's own children may now shrink, but a grid item's
   automatic minimum is its min-content width, and .experiment-list and
   .approval-list are both display: grid — so the track sizes itself to the
   string. .opportunity-list is not a grid at all, and there the same string
   simply overflows an ordinary block child that refuses to break. Measured at
   a 375px viewport: 581px of document scrollWidth on / and /experiments, 587px
   on /opportunities, on every width from 320 to 414.
   min-width: 0 on the list items is deliberately NOT added: a box that stops
   growing does not make its content break, and it still measured 564px.
   anywhere rather than break-word, because break-word adds the break
   opportunity but leaves intrinsic sizing alone — the grid track above is
   still floored at the string's min-content width, and /experiments kept
   measuring 581px with it.
   Scoped to the three card lists rather than applied to #main, because a
   blanket overflow-wrap reaches the table cells and makes every wide table
   wrap to its column instead of scrolling in the region #48 gave it: measured,
   /journal's region collapsed from 755>278 to 278>278, as did every region on
   /. The cure would have undone the fix, and no test could see it. */
.experiment-card,
.opportunity-row,
.approval-card,
.experiment-card *,
.opportunity-row *,
.approval-card * {
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
--- NEW
/* A free-text name on an experiment, opportunity, approval or research
   observation is one unbreakable token, and one long enough token still
   scrolls the page sideways even with the floor lifted above: a grid item's
   automatic minimum is its min-content width, and .experiment-list and
   .approval-list are both display: grid, so the track sizes to the string.
   `anywhere` rather than `break-word`, which leaves intrinsic sizing alone.
   Scoped to these four lists, never to #main: a blanket wrap reaches the
   table cells and makes every wide table wrap instead of scrolling in its
   own region. No `*` descendants — overflow-wrap is inherited. */
.experiment-card,
.opportunity-row,
.approval-card,
.learning-card {
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

(2) Replace this block — the bare .tenant-name rule at src/web/styles.css:103-105 — with the new text in its place. min-width: 0 is declared before overflow-wrap so the two read in the order they matter:

--- OLD
.tenant-name {
